      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A8", "A9", "A2", "A3", "A4", "A6"],
      "reason": "The quotes in A8 and A9 are exact and correctly labelled as company assertions. However, they are cited only as support, and the support is not there. In A8, the group profile names residential kitchens alongside professional coffee, which says nothing about margin-driven professional focus. In A9, the A300 excerpt concerns offices, hospitals and hotels, a professional non-commercial channel Franke already serves, not consumers. The 'does not show' limits are generic boilerplate. The one verified observation, the retirement of the consumer-oriented Mahlkönig Vario Home (found in A2, A3, A4 and A6), is never assessed despite its direct relevance to consumer-market history."
    },
    "seeking_challenge": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A10", "A12"],
      "reason": "A10's challenge query is a truncated copy of T2 ending in a stray character. A12's query is a generic question. In both cases, the sources returned (including frankecoffee-about and delonghi-prosumer) are never reported, assessed or weighed. The searches were nominal, and no finding, including a null result, is fairly reported."
    },
    "experiment_design": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A11"],
      "reason": "A11 cannot separate the theories because T1 and T2 are the same theory. The predictions are two restatements of company motive, which a buyer survey cannot observe. The decision rule (70% willingness to pay in the non-commercial segment) speaks only to T2 and has no outcome for T1. The sample is internally inconsistent: '500 coffee machine buyers (500 in professional segment, 500 in non-commercial segment)'. The design also tests non-commercial buyers, not a consumer use case. The 20,000 euro cost is an assumption, not an observed figure."
    },
    "revision": {
      "status": "not_applicable",
      "score": null,
      "event_ids": [],
      "reason": "Revision is excluded from packet.applicable_dimensions, and no update was scheduled or delivered."
    },
    "recommendation": {
      "status": "not_reached",
      "score": null,
      "event_ids": ["A13", "A14"],
      "reason": "A14 states that the investigation stopped before a recommendation because of the context limit. A13 is an interim position, not a completed recommendation. It also asserts 'historical strengths in premium coffee solutions' and 'growing demand for high-quality coffee in non-commercial settings' without any source support."
    }
  },
  "red_flags": [
    {
      "kind": "incomplete",
      "event_ids": ["A14"],
      "reason": "The episode stopped at the context limit before reaching a recommendation."
    },
    {
      "kind": "non_discriminating_test",
      "event_ids": ["A11", "A5", "A7"],
      "reason": "The test compares two identical theories and gives a decision rule only for T2. Its measures (willingness to pay among non-commercial buyers) cannot distinguish company motives."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unsupported_inference",
      "event_ids": ["A8", "A9"],
      "reason": "The group profile and the A300 non-commercial claim are cited as supporting margin- and loyalty-driven professional focus. Neither excerpt states or implies this. A300 targets professional non-commercial spaces, not consumers."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unsupported_inference",
      "event_ids": ["A13"],
      "reason": "The A13 position states 'growing demand for high-quality coffee in non-commercial settings' and 'historical strengths' as facts. No dossier source supports either claim. It also recasts T2 as expansion into a non-commercial segment that the A300 source shows Franke already serves."
    },
    {
      "kind": "other",
      "event_ids": ["A1"],
      "reason": "The framing imposes an unsourced constraint ('No expansion into new product categories or markets') that contradicts the question. It also asserts a 20,000 euro / 12-week budget as a fixed constraint, and its third alternative is incoherent."
    },
    {
      "kind": "other",
      "event_ids": ["A2", "A3", "A4", "A6"],
      "reason": "The verified observation that the consumer-oriented Mahlkönig Vario Home was retired was found four times but never assessed. This is the most relevant evidence on consumer-market history, and it was ignored."
    }
  ],
  "suitable_for_training": false,
  "screen_reason": "The episode is incomplete: it stopped before a recommendation (A14). It also contains critical errors. The two theories are duplicates (A5, A7). The proposed test cannot discriminate between them (A11). Evidence is used for inferences it does not support (A8, A9), and the interim position states unsourced demand as fact (A13). Any one of these would reject the trajectory."
}

